351→/// The generics T and R represent additional metric information that can exist, both for individual queries and the test run as a whole
352→/// T and R may not always be equal, as the test run may have different metrics than the individual queries
353→///
354→/// For example, the throughput test uses ``NoExtendedMetrics`` for the individual queries, but ``ThroughputMetrics`` for the test run
355→pub struct QueryMetrics<T: ExtendedMetrics, R: ExtendedMetrics> {
356→    pub run_id: Uuid,
